{"parentUuid":"7408dea4-21d1-4614-b90a-6fb2b98da7f5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CeakNGdDjPLtc8TyECAEJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Scan done (throwaway instance stopped, `scan.db` removed; your main console on 18080 is untouched). I drove headless Chrome across every view. Here's what I found, in plain English — **I've fixed nothing; tell me which to do and how.**\n\n## Cross-cutting (affects the whole console)\n1. **Three different list styles.** Datasets is now a clean, aligned, borderless table — but **Runs** is bordered cards and **Templates** is cards-with-a-header. They look like three different apps. Candidate: unify Runs + Templates to the same table style as Datasets.\n2. **Inconsistent number formatting.** The Datasets table shows comma-grouped counts with no unit word (\"1,500,000\"). But **Runs** still says \"1702000 rows\", the **dataset detail** says \"1500000 / 1500000\" and \"1500000 rows\", and **lineage tooltips** say \"1500000 row(s)\". These should all be comma-grouped, and drop the redundant \"rows/run\" wherever a column or label already says it.\n\n## Datasets list\n3. The **DATASET cell cuts the URI mid-character** with no visible \"…\" or fade — it *is* scrollable, but there's no cue that there's more (just a thin scrollbar). A soft right-edge fade would signal \"scroll for more.\"\n\n## Dataset detail\n4. **Local outputs is still card-style**, so the green PRESENT badge, the age/date, and the action buttons **don't line up** between rows (the misalignment you spotted). Same table treatment would fix it.\n5. **\"Volume (recent runs)\" looks broken with one run** — a single thin bar in a big empty box. With sparse data it reads as an error. Could show a friendlier empty state (or hide it) until there are a few runs.\n6. The detail's own numbers (\"ROWS (LAST/TOTAL)\", the UPSTREAM box) aren't comma-grouped and repeat \"rows/run\" — same as #2.\n7. The **management controls row** (show cleaned · days · Purge · Clean · refresh) is cramped — could tuck behind a small \"Manage\" disclosure so the default view is just the outputs + preview.\n\n## Lineage\n8. **Right-column node labels get clipped** at the right edge of the graph card (e.g., \"…salesforce__opportunity_line_item\" is cut off) — the graph overflows its container with no horizontal scroll, so the right nodes' names are unreadable at the tail.\n9. Every node shows only the URI tail with a \"…\" prefix; for the salesforce rows the shared \"…faucet_stream.salesforce__\" prefix repeats on every node and eats space — minor, but the distinguishing part is squeezed.\n\nWhich of these do you want, and any specific direction (e.g., \"unify all lists to the table\", \"keep Volume but fix empty state\")? I'll implement only what you green-light."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1994,"cache_read_input_tokens":813812,"output_tokens":1013,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":71},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1994,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1013,"cache_read_input_tokens":813812,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1994,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1994},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeakMzh1tPsouvPT4WmCg","type":"assistant","uuid":"e3a32faf-c8f6-4542-a6b6-f102d23c1774","timestamp":"2026-08-31T11:29:30.756Z","effort":"high","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.231","gitBranch":"feat/native-byte-passthrough-633","slug":"l