{"parentUuid":"619ffe0f-010a-4e1b-88ca-c031140be1be","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CeamSXuThfGspEzQbHMv9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MDV74PSkXb4GMqot1bD6sk","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream/CLAUDE.md","old_string":"```bash\ncargo test --workspace --all-features\ncargo test -p faucet-core\ncargo test -p faucet-stream --features full\n```\n\n## Dependency Policy","new_string":"```bash\ncargo test --workspace --all-features\ncargo test -p faucet-core\ncargo test -p faucet-stream --features full\n```\n\n## Live UI verification (serve web console / `serve-ui`)\n\n**For any non-trivial change to the web console (`cli/src/serve/ui/**` — JS/CSS/HTML), verify it in a real rendered browser, not just by reading the code.** A CSS/layout change that looks fine in source routinely breaks in ways only a render reveals (sticky-header gaps, per-row grids that don't align across rows, `background` shorthands that reset `background-repeat` and tile an image, scrollbars overlapping text, dark-mode-only glitches). The cost of a headless render pass is minutes; the cost of shipping a visibly-broken console is a round-trip with the user each time.\n\nStandard loop:\n\n1. **Serve the assets from disk.** In a debug build `rust-embed` serves `cli/src/serve/ui/**` from disk at request time, so **JS/CSS/HTML edits go live on the running `faucet serve` with just a browser refresh — no rebuild.** Only Rust changes (handlers, features like `templates`/`catalog`) need a rebuild + restart.\n2. **Render every affected view with headless Chrome** and actually **look at the screenshots** (via the Read tool). Drive a throwaway `--no-auth` copy of the server so no token injection is needed:\n   ```bash\n   cp <history>.db /tmp/scan.db\n   ./target/debug/faucet serve --listen 127.0.0.1:18081 --no-auth --history sqlite:/tmp/scan.db --preview-local-outputs &\n   CHROME=\"/Applications/Google Chrome.app/Contents/MacOS/Google Chrome\"\n   \"$CHROME\" --headless --disable-gpu --force-device-scale-factor=2 --window-size=1500,1300 \\\n     --virtual-time-budget=7000 --screenshot=/tmp/view.png \"http://127.0.0.1:18081/#/catalog\"\n   ```\n   Routes are hash-based (`#/runs`, `#/catalog`, `#/catalog/{id}`, `#/lineage`, `#/templates`, `#/schemas`, `#/submit`).\n3. **Check BOTH themes.** The console has light/dark/auto (`localStorage['faucet.theme']` → `data-theme` on `<html>`, dark also via `@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)` on `[data-theme=auto]`). Add `--force-dark-mode` to the Chrome invocation for the dark pass. Several bugs are dark-only.\n4. **Exercise the clickables**, not just the static page: open dropdowns/menus, expand the preview panel, toggle Preview↔Hide, hover rows (tooltips), scroll long lists (sticky headers), and click a lineage node. Many defects only appear in an interactive state.\n5. **Verify the served asset actually changed** before claiming done (`curl …/assets/views/<x>.js | grep <marker>`), then confirm the render.\n\nReuse `.ds-table` (the shared aligned/sticky table) for list views rather than per-row grids — independent per-row grids do not align columns across rows. Keep number formatting consistent via `fmtInt` in `utils.js` (comma-grouped, no redundant \"rows\"/\"run\" when a column/label already says it).\n\n## Dependency Policy"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":229,"cache_read_input_tokens":868847,"output_tokens":1358,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":229,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1358,"cache_read_input_tokens":868847,"cache_creation_input_tokens":229,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":229},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeamSCg4jkkN6zPqBBfgm","type":"assistant","uuid":"e316f335-8da3-4a12-8a1e-13126698c866","timestamp":"2026-08-31T11:43:41.167Z","effort":"high","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.231","gitBranch":"feat/native-byte-passthrough-633","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
